---
import SiteLayout from '../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';

const siteUrl = 'https://shadowharness.github.io/';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const pageUrl = `${siteUrl}en/guide/`;
const title = 'ShadowHarness Guide — One desk and one memory for your AI agents';
const description =
	'ShadowHarness is an integrated LLM terminal for Windows that brings Codex, Claude Code, Grok, Gemini, and more into one workspace with shared memory.';
---

<SiteLayout
	lang="en"
	title={title}
	description={description}
	pageUrl={pageUrl}
	alternateJa={`${siteUrl}guide/`}
	alternateEn={pageUrl}
>
	<main id="main-content" class="guide-page" tabindex="-1">
		<header class="guide-hero">
			<p class="eyebrow">PRODUCT GUIDE</p>
			<h1>ShadowHarness Guide</h1>
			<p class="lead">One desk and one memory for your AI agents.</p>
			<p>
				ShadowHarness is an integrated LLM terminal and agent desktop for Windows. It brings
				multiple AI agents, files, previews, and memory into one working surface.
			</p>
			<div class="cta-row">
				<a class="cta primary" href={`${base}en/#demo`}>Watch the demo</a>
				<a class="cta ghost" href="https://x.com/ShadowHarness" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
					Follow development on X
				</a>
			</div>
		</header>

		<div class="guide-layout">
			<aside class="guide-nav">
				<p>In this guide</p>
				<nav aria-label="Guide contents">
					<a href="#overview">What ShadowHarness is</a>
					<a href="#agents">Use your usual AIs</a>
					<a href="#workspace">One working surface</a>
					<a href="#memory">Sidera Memory</a>
					<a href="#workflow">A typical workflow</a>
					<a href="#status">Status and updates</a>
				</nav>
			</aside>

			<article class="guide-content prose">
				<section id="overview">
					<p class="eyebrow">01 / OVERVIEW</p>
					<h2>A desk for AI work, built on Windows</h2>
					<p>
						As you add more AI agents, conversations spread across terminals, project files
						live in other windows, and results open in still more apps. ShadowHarness brings
						those pieces together on one working surface.
					</p>
					<div class="guide-callout">
						<strong>Use GPT / Codex, Claude Code, Grok, Gemini, and more as they are.</strong>{' '}
						Bring the agents you already know onto one working surface with a shared desk and memory.
					</div>
					<dl class="facts-list">
						<div>
							<dt>One desk</dt>
							<dd>Keep multiple AIs, files, previews, and editing in the same window.</dd>
						</div>
						<div>
							<dt>One job</dt>
							<dd>Give agents different roles while they work against the same project.</dd>
						</div>
						<div>
							<dt>One memory</dt>
							<dd>Carry forward the relevant past instead of dragging an entire conversation along.</dd>
						</div>
					</dl>
				</section>

				<section id="agents">
					<p class="eyebrow">02 / AGENTS</p>
					<h2>GPT / Codex, Claude Code, Grok, Gemini, and more — as they are</h2>
					<p>
						The agents inside ShadowHarness are the tools you already know. You can place
						Codex beside Claude Code and assign each a different role, then bring in Grok or
						Gemini when another perspective helps.
					</p>
				</section>

				<section id="workspace">
					<p class="eyebrow">03 / WORKSPACE</p>
					<h2>Keep thinking and making on the same surface</h2>
					<div class="trust-grid">
						<div>
							<h3>Multiple AI panes</h3>
							<p>
								Open the agents you need and arrange them as the job changes. Put one on
								research, one on implementation, and another on review while keeping the
								whole effort visible.
							</p>
						</div>
						<div>
							<h3>Explorer</h3>
							<p>
								Browse the project's folders and files, then bring the right target into
								an agent or Preview. The state of the work stays visible outside the chat.
							</p>
						</div>
						<div>
							<h3>Preview / Editor</h3>
							<p>
								Inspect text, images, audio, and video without leaving the workspace. Edit
								text in place, and move between source and rendered Markdown or HTML.
							</p>
						</div>
					</div>
				</section>

				<section id="memory">
					<p class="eyebrow">04 / SIDERA MEMORY</p>
					<h2>Turn stored history into memory the next task can use</h2>
					<p>
						Each CLI already leaves raw conversation logs on your PC. But keeping history is
						not the same as giving the next agent the part it needs. Resuming one long thread
						carries growing context forward, while switching agents or sessions fragments the
						reasoning behind a decision.
					</p>
					<p>
						Sidera Memory organizes new log data through Shadow Hub and selects only the past
						that relates to the current input. It does not flatten a conversation into a
						disposable short summary: it preserves which conclusion is current, what changed,
						and where the supporting evidence can be traced in the original record.
					</p>
					<div class="guide-callout">
						<strong>
							Not just what was remembered, but what the current conclusion is, how it
							changed, and what supports it.
						</strong>{' '}
						That is the role of memory in ShadowHarness.
					</div>
					<ol>
						<li>Each AI's raw conversation log remains where its CLI stores it on your PC.</li>
						<li>New log ranges are sent to Shadow Hub and structured into memory with LLM judgment.</li>
						<li>Only memory relevant to the next input is selected and delivered to the working agent.</li>
						<li>When needed, the structured result can point back to evidence in the original record.</li>
					</ol>
					<p>
						See <a href={`${base}en/security/`}>Data Handling &amp; Trust</a> for the boundary
						between your device, Shadow Hub, and the LLM used for this processing.
					</p>
				</section>

				<section id="workflow">
					<p class="eyebrow">05 / WORKFLOW</p>
					<h2>Move one request forward with several AIs</h2>
					<ol>
						<li>
							<strong>Open the project.</strong>{' '}
							Find the target in Explorer and arrange the agents you need in panes.
						</li>
						<li>
							<strong>Divide the roles.</strong>{' '}
							Assign research, implementation, and review to different agents while
							watching their progress on one screen.
						</li>
						<li>
							<strong>Inspect the result in place.</strong>{' '}
							Open changed files in Preview and make your own edits in the Editor when needed.
						</li>
						<li>
							<strong>Continue in a fresh session.</strong>{' '}
							Instead of carrying the entire chat, Sidera Memory supplies conclusions and
							history relevant to the new input.
						</li>
					</ol>
					<p>
						Choose the AI that fits each part of the job, while the desk and memory stay
						shared. That is the working environment ShadowHarness provides.
					</p>
				</section>

				<section id="status">
					<p class="eyebrow">06 / STATUS</p>
					<h2>ShadowHarness today</h2>
					<p>
						The demo on the home page shows the current interface and behavior. Development
						updates and future tester opportunities will be announced on this site or the
						official X account after their details and timing are confirmed.
					</p>
					<div class="guide-callout">
						<a href={`${base}en/#demo`}>Watch the demo</a>
						<span aria-hidden="true"> · </span>
						<a href="https://x.com/ShadowHarness" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
							Follow @ShadowHarness
						</a>
					</div>
				</section>
			</article>
		</div>
	</main>
</SiteLayout>
